      "## Definitions\n\nWrite the start event, the stop event, the pause rule, and the treatment of missing evidence. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nDefine the primary measure and one supporting measure. Use the same definitions for every case. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nIf a definition changes, keep the earlier classification and apply the new rule only to later cases. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nWhen evidence is unavailable, record that state instead of leaving a blank. Missing and confirmed negative are different. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nWrite the next action with an owner and a time. \"Review the exception\" is not a next action; a named person checking a named source by a stated time is. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nClose the loop with the requester. Internal completeness without confirmation is only half closed. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nName a backup owner for leave and time-zone gaps. Coverage should be written into the routine. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.",
      "## Evidence and data dictionary\n\nEach case needs the source, the time observed, the field supported, and the reviewer. Mark missing, unavailable, and confirmed negative values separately. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nUse a pseudonymous key and keep the identity crosswalk in an approved system. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nRecord the source version so a later reviewer can tell what was known at the first action. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nUse a short reason code for each exception. The code should describe the evidence problem, not the person. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nKeep the payment run queue separate from the general inbox. A queue without an owner hides the oldest item. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nRecord the payment run source and observation time. A later reviewer should be able to tell whether the value was current when the first action was taken. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nDo not copy a value because it looks familiar. Reopen the source and record what changed. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.",
      "## Sampling\n\nUse consecutive cases where possible and stratify by channel, owner, or risk class. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nInclude adverse cases: missing source, conflicting instruction, unavailable owner, and a tight deadline. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nRecord the eligible count, sample size, and every exclusion so the sample can be reproduced. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nReview one payment run case end to end in the weekly meeting. Check the source, decision, destination record, and confirmation. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nWhen evidence is unavailable, record that state instead of leaving a blank. Missing and confirmed negative are different. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nWrite the next action with an owner and a time. \"Review the exception\" is not a next action; a named person checking a named source by a stated time is. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nClose the loop with the requester. Internal completeness without confirmation is only half closed. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.",
      "## Analysis\n\nReport the missing-field rate, the exception rate, the unresolved count, and the age of open cases. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nSeparate observation from interpretation. A small easy sample is not evidence of a strong control. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nKeep case-level detail available for review. A summary chart without records cannot support a decision. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nIf the rule changes, keep the earlier classification and apply the new rule to later cases. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nUse a short reason code for each exception. The code should describe the evidence problem, not the person. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nKeep the payment run queue separate from the general inbox. A queue without an owner hides the oldest item. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.\n\nRecord the payment run source and observation time. A later reviewer should be able to tell whether the value was current when the first action was taken. This applies to outsourceaccountspayable-testing-handoff-completeness-in-payment-run.",
